Tcl in bext
===========

Bext builds Tcl from the complete upstream source distribution mirrored by the
RELEASE branch of BRL-CAD/tcl.  The Tcl core Git tags are not sufficient for
this purpose: release assembly adds the packages under pkgs, including Itcl.
Tcl 8.6.18 supplies Itcl 4.3.7 there.  Configuration fails immediately if the
declared Itcl source directory is absent, rather than allowing the later Itk
build to fail with incomplete private headers or configuration data.

The bundled Itcl version and the minimum system version are deliberately
separate.  The source distribution determines the former.  The latter is the
oldest version that passes BRL-CAD and upstream Itk compatibility testing, so
a newer Tcl release does not by itself raise the requirement imposed on a
complete system Tcl/Tk/Itcl/Itk stack.

zlib selection
--------------

The Tcl source distribution also contains a fallback zlib implementation in
compat/zlib.  That is useful to Tcl's normal standalone build, but it can hide
an incomplete external-zlib setup by supplying headers or sources after bext
has selected its symbol-prefixed z_brl library.

On Unix-like platforms, when bext builds zlib locally, Tcl's configure probe is
patched to require brl_deflateSetHeader from z_brl.  Bext then removes
compat/zlib only from the ExternalProject staging copy.  Consequently Tcl must
compile with the installed z_brl headers and library, and a bad include path
fails instead of silently mixing the distribution headers with z_brl.  The Tcl
source submodule remains an unmodified copy of the official distribution.

When a local z_brl target is not present, bext leaves the fallback directory
and upstream zlib selection unchanged.  The removal is also intentionally not
part of the Windows build: Tcl's Windows makefiles use files supplied by the
distribution's compatibility zlib tree.

Validation
----------

A bundled-stack build must establish all of the following:

* the Tcl staging tree has no compat/zlib when z_brl is selected;
* Tcl's configure probe resolves brl_deflateSetHeader from -lz_brl;
* the installed Tcl library depends on libz_brl and has unresolved brl_ zlib
  symbols for that library to satisfy;
* package require reports Itcl 4.3.7, Itk 4.2.7, and Iwidgets 4.1.1; and
* Itk's upstream suite and BRL-CAD's Tcl GUI baseline pass under Xmin.
